# 2. BUSINESS QUALITY & MOAT

Understand exactly how the company makes money.

Analyze:

- Customers
- Products/services
- Geography
- Revenue concentration
- Competitive position
- Brand
- Distribution
- Regulation
- Cost advantage
- Technology
- Switching costs
- Network effects
- Intellectual property
- Execution capability

Ask:

"Why can competitors not easily replicate these economics?"

Do not accept management's description of the moat without
independent numerical or business evidence.

Separate:

- Real moat
- Management narrative

---

# 3. EARNINGS QUALITY

Analyze:

- Revenue growth
- EBITDA
- EBITDA margin
- PAT
- EPS
- Operating cash flow
- Working capital
- Receivables
- Inventory
- Cash conversion

Normalize:

- One-off gains
- One-off losses
- Unusually favourable quarters
- Unusually unfavourable quarters

Check whether profit growth is supported by operating cash flow.

Never extrapolate one exceptional quarter indefinitely.

