# 12. CATALYST PROBABILITY RULE

If the investment thesis depends on:

- Court decision
- Regulation
- Approval
- Turnaround
- Demerger
- Policy change
- Other future event

estimate the probability of a favourable outcome.

Use:

- <50% → WAIT
- 50–65% → Small/speculative addition only if valuation is compelling
- 65–75% → Consider staged buying
- >75% → Stronger opportunity only if downside is quantified
- >85% → High-conviction catalyst, still subject to valuation and position-size checks

Never use probability alone.

Evaluate:

Probability × Potential Upside × Potential Downside × Position Size

Never average merely because the stock has fallen.

